From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: a drain waits for the pictures its end
 code pushes out

A drain queues the codec's end-of-stream sequence, which pushes the
pictures the microcode still holds through, then waits until the
decoder has been without an interrupt for 50 ms. The wait counted from
the last interrupt before the drain: after a client had been quiet for
longer, the drain ended at once and flagged LAST before the microcode
decoded what the sequence pushed out. A 3-picture 1080p MPEG-4 stream,
queued whole and stopped a second later, gave 1 or 2 pictures.

Count the quiet from the moment the sequence is queued.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 vdec/vdec.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -461,6 +461,8 @@
 
 		/* push the last picture through, then let it decode */
 		esparser_queue_eos(sess->core, data, len);
+		/* the quiet that ends the drain starts now, not at the last interrupt */
+		sess->last_irq_jiffies = get_jiffies_64();
 		if (codec_ops->eos_queued)
 			codec_ops->eos_queued(sess);
 		vdec_wait_eos_decoded(sess, len);
